[[lookup]]
****
xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]

. If ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else if let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``:
 .. Check that ``K~h~`` is equal to ``K~query~``.

 .. Return ``V~h~``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Check that ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` is a non-empty list.

  ... Let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Return ``xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]``.
****

=== Shorthands

[#option_get]
==== Force-unwrap (`?`)

Force-unwraps an optional. If the value is none, the rule does not apply.

== Static semantics

The typing judgments characterise well-formed expressions and commands
under a typing context that maps each in-scope variable to its declared
type.

=== Expressions

