[[Check_expr]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Check_expr[Check_expr: ``tenv ⊢ expr +++:+++ %``]
****

ifdef::backend-html5[]
.Click to view the specification source
[%collapsible]
====
----
rule Check_expr/num:
  tenv |- (_NUM i) : INT

rule Check_expr/boollit:
  tenv |- (_BOOL b) : BOOL

rule Check_expr/id:
  tenv |- x : t
 -- if $lookup<id, type>(tenv, x) = t

rule Check_expr/not:
  tenv |- ! e : BOOL
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e : BOOL

rule Check_expr/add:
  tenv |- e_l + e_r : INT
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_l : INT
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_r : INT

rule Check_expr/leq:
  tenv |- e_l <= e_r : BOOL
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_l : INT
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_r : INT

rule Check_expr/and:
  tenv |- e_l && e_r : BOOL
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_l : BOOL
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_r : BOOL

rule Check_expr/fun:
  tenv |- FUN `(t_arg x_arg) -> t_ret `{e} : t_arg -> t_ret
 -- Check_expr: ((x_arg -> t_arg) :: tenv) |- e : t_ret

rule Check_expr/call:
  tenv |- (e_f `(e_a)) : t_ret
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_f : t_arg -> t_ret
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e_a : t_arg
----
====

[.empty]
--


--

endif::[]

****
. If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
 .. If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let~xref:option_get[?]~ ``t`` be ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]``.
 .. Result in ``t``.
. Else if let ``+++!+++ e`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.

 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++++++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.

 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.

 .. Result in ``+++INT+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++<=+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.

 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.

 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++&&+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.

 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.

 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``+++FUN+++ +++(+++t~arg~ x~arg~+++)+++ +++->+++ t~ret~ +++{+++e+++}+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``x~arg~ → t~arg~ {two-colons} tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t~ret~``.

 .. Result in ``t~arg~ +++->+++ t~ret~``.
. Else if let ``e~f~ +++(+++e~a~+++)+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~f~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``t~arg~ +++->+++ t~ret~`` be ``type``.

 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~a~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` is equal to ``t~arg~``.

 .. Result in ``t~ret~``.
****

