****
xref:Check_command[Check_command: ``tenv ⊢ command ⊣ %``]
****

ifdef::backend-html5[]
.Click to view the specification source
[%collapsible]
====
----
rule Check_command/skip:
  tenv |- SKIP -| tenv

rule Check_command/decl:
  tenv |- (t x = e) -| (x -> t) :: tenv
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e : t

rule Check_command/assign:
  tenv |- (x = e) -| tenv
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e : t
 -- if $lookup<id, type>(tenv, x) = t

rule Check_command/ite:
  tenv |- (IF e THEN c_1 ELSE c_2 END) -| tenv
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e : BOOL
 -- Check_command: tenv |- c_1 -| tenv_1
 -- Check_command: tenv |- c_2 -| tenv_2

rule Check_command/while:
  tenv |- (WHILE e DO c END) -| tenv
 -- Check_expr: tenv |- e : BOOL
 -- Check_command: tenv |- c -| tenv_1

rule Check_command/seq:
  tenv |- (c_1 ; c_2) -| tenv_2
 -- Check_command: tenv |- c_1 -| tenv_1
 -- Check_command: tenv_1 |- c_2 -| tenv_2
----
====

[.empty]
--


--

endif::[]

****
. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+++SKIP+++``:
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``t x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``x → t {two-colons} tenv``.
. Else if let ``x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ t``].
 .. Check that ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]`` is equal to ``t``.

 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+++IF+++ e +++THEN+++ c~1~ +++ELSE+++ c~2~ +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.

 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+++WHILE+++ e +++DO+++ c +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.

 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +++;+++ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv~1~ ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv~2~``.
****

== Dynamic semantics

The evaluation judgments give a big-step semantics. Expressions reduce
to values; commands transform an environment to an environment.

=== Expressions

