endif::[]

[[Eval_expr]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Eval_expr[Eval_expr: ``env ⊢ expr ⟹ %``]
****

ifdef::backend-html5[]
.Click to view the specification source
[%collapsible]
====
----
rule Eval_expr/num:
  env |- (_NUM i) ==> (_NUM i)

rule Eval_expr/boollit:
  env |- (_BOOL b) ==> (_BOOL b)

rule Eval_expr/id:
  env |- x ==> v
 -- if $lookup<id, value>(env, x) = v

rule Eval_expr/not:
  env |- (! e) ==> (_BOOL b)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e ==> (_BOOL b_e)
 -- if b = ~b_e

rule Eval_expr/add:
  env |- (e_l + e_r) ==> (_NUM i)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_l ==> (_NUM i_l)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_r ==> (_NUM i_r)
 -- if i = i_l + i_r

rule Eval_expr/leq:
  env |- (e_l <= e_r) ==> (_BOOL b)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_l ==> (_NUM i_l)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_r ==> (_NUM i_r)
 -- if b = i_l <= i_r

rule Eval_expr/and:
  env |- (e_l && e_r) ==> (_BOOL b)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_l ==> (_BOOL b_l)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_r ==> (_BOOL b_r)
 -- if b = (b_l /\ b_r)

rule Eval_expr/fun:
  env |- (FUN `(t_arg x_arg) -> t_ret `{e}) ==> (CLO x_arg e env)

rule Eval_expr/call:
  env |- (e_f `(e_a)) ==> v_ret
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_f ==> (CLO x_a e_body env_clo)
 -- Eval_expr: env |- e_a ==> v
 -- Eval_expr: ((x_a -> v) :: env_clo) |- e_body ==> v_ret
----
====

[.empty]
--


--

endif::[]

****
. If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
 .. If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``i``.
 .. Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let~xref:option_get[?]~ ``v`` be ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, value>(env, x)]``.
 .. Result in ``v``.
. Else if let ``+++!+++ e`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``b~e~`` be ``literal``.

 .. Let ``b`` be not ``b~e~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++++++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

 .. Let ``i`` be ``i~l~`` + ``i~r~``.
 .. Result in ``i``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++<=+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.

 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.

 .. Let ``b`` be ``i~l~`` is less than or equal to ``i~r~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++&&+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal`` be ``value``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``b~l~`` be ``literal``.

 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``b~r~`` be ``literal'``.

 .. Let ``b`` be ``b~l~`` and ``b~r~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``+++FUN+++ +++(+++t~arg~ x~arg~+++)+++ +++->+++ t~ret~ +++{+++e+++}+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Result in ``+++CLO+++ x~arg~ e env``.
. Else if let ``e~f~ +++(+++e~a~+++)+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~f~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``+++CLO+++ x~a~ e~body~ env~clo~`` be ``value``.

 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~a~ ⟹ v``].
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``x~a~ → v {two-colons} env~clo~ ⊢ e~body~ ⟹ v~ret~``].
 .. Result in ``v~ret~``.
****

